                <pb facs="0733" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg625"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 10, 1893.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson announces the return of Mr. Newberry, whose report affords a
                    sufficient basis for the folio wing demands: The issuance of an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">iradé</hi> in favor of the school, the assurance of
                    adequate protection, the immediate granting of a permit to build, and the
                    payment of 500 Turkish pounds, value of the destroyed building, and requests
                    instructions.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
